<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Unit 4 Section C Overview: A Closer Look at Inputs and Outputs</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01062</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Unit 4 Section C Overview: A Closer Look at Inputs and Outputs</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f9b75dd9-c74a-4d61-ba09-12bfe6e3b37b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Mr. Das has been interested in how batteries work and how to make them last longer since he was a boy. Now he is using that interest as a PhD candidate at MIT to produce longer-lasting batteries, which can cut down the impact on the environment. He can use functions to help him analyze energy inputs and outputs as he studies battery power and efficiency.</para>
<para>In this section, you will take a closer look at the input and output of a function. You will learn to identify the domain, inputs, and range, outputs, of a function based on context and graphs.</para>
<para>This section includes 2 lessons:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    4.12 Domain and Range, Part 1</item>
  <item>
    4.13 Domain and Range, Part 2</item>
</list>

